					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/bronzegauntlets" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2085647); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2085647&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238218" alt="bronzegauntlets" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2085647)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/bronzegauntlets" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2085647); return false;" >bronzegauntlets</a></span> <span class="odate time_1551056059 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">25 Feb 2019 00:54</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4164447">
									

<p>There are a few problems that made me dislike this article.</p>
<p>The exploration log, to me, was too long, and it didn't keep my interest. I'm not sure that the temple itself was important to the overall story of the article.</p>
<p>My main problem with the article was that I don't really see how the species is anomalous. Big flying arachnids with above-average intelligence are weird, but they don't do anything outside of mainstream reality, unless I'm missing something. Also&#8212; we don't get a good idea of <em>how</em> big the creatures are, (again) unless I missed something.</p>
<p>The concept might be lost on me because I'm not that scared of the creepy-crawlies, but I think that my analysis stands regardless.</p>
<p>-1</p>

